  "database": "rschema_0307",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0307 database is designed to store information about companies, their employees, and various related entities. The Companies_Table stores details about each company, including its unique identifier, name, website, creation and update dates. The API_Keys_Table holds information about API keys, such as the reason for their creation, creation and update dates, a unique identifier, name, private key, and URI. The Employees_Table contains data about employees, including their company affiliation, creation and update dates, a unique identifier, name, position, and salary. The Sites_Table stores details about various sites, including their creation and update dates, database name, hostname, whether they are deprecated, abbreviation, name, and a unique identifier. The Devices_Table holds information about devices, such as their associated employee, creation and update dates, and a unique identifier. The Users_Table stores user account information, including their company affiliation, creation and update dates, display name usage, email, whether they are an administrator or developer, last login time, password, password salt, password type, real name, a unique identifier, username, and a foreign key referencing the Sites_Table to establish the site they belong to, with the Site_ID column being a non-nullable foreign key.",
  "gold_question": "The requirements analysis for the company's internal management system is as follows:  \n\nCompany Management:  \nStore company information, including Company ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Company Website, and Company Name. The Company Name is unique. Operations include adding, modifying, and deleting company information, such as the company name and website.  \n\nUser Management:  \nStore user information, including User ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Is Admin, Real Name, Password Type, Password Salt, Username, Email, Password, Display Name Usage, Is Developer, and Last Login Time. The Username and Email are unique. Operations include registering new users, modifying user information, setting admin and developer roles, and recording the last login time. A company can have multiple users.  \n\nAPI Key Management:  \nStore API key information, including Key ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Private Key, Application Reason, Key Name, and URI. The Key Name is unique and is associated with the user table. A user can only have one API key. Users can apply for an API key and provide a reason for the application.  \n\nEmployee Management:  \nStore employee information, including Employee ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Employee Name, Position, and Salary. This is associated with the company table, and a company can have multiple employees. Operations include managing employee information such as name, position, and salary, as well as assigning employees to different companies.  \n\nSite Management:  \nStore site information, including Site ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Database Name, Is Deprecated, Site Name, Hostname, and Site Abbreviation. The Database Name and Site Abbreviation are unique and are associated with the user table. A user can only use one site. Operations include managing site information such as site name, hostname, and site abbreviation, as well as marking sites as deprecated.  \n\nDevice Management:  \nStore device information, including Device ID, Creation Date, Update Date, Device Name, and Associated Employee ID. This is associated with the employee table, and an employee can manage multiple devices.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0307.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0307\nCREATE TABLE `companies_table` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_keys_table` (\n  `api_key_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `private_key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `uri` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reason` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`api_key_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employees_table` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employees_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `companies_table` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sites_table` (\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `hostname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `database_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_deprecated` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `abbreviation` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`site_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `devices_table` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `devices_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employees_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users_table` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_admin` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `is_developer` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `last_login` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_salt` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `real_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `sites_table` (`site_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `users_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `companies_table` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
